  "rationale": "The defining Verve-era leader date from the father of the tenor saxophone. Coleman Hawkins is the foundational figure of the jazz tenor tradition, yet appears in the canon only via a single encounter album with Ben Webster. This 1957 session pairs Hawk with Oscar Peterson's crack quartet for an album of standards that showcases his harmonically advanced, tough-toned playing \u2014 a direct bridge from the swing era into the mainstream hard-bop tradition. Penguin Guide 3.5 stars, AllMusic 4 stars. Session gravity: Peterson, Ellis, Brown, Stoller = the premier small-group rhythm section of the late 1950s. Consensus classic across Penguin, AllMusic, and Verve's own catalogue canon.",
